{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"partSymbol"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<part-symbol>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/partsymbol"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part-symbol element indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"partSymbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"partSymbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAttributesV10partSymbolAA07MXLPartE0VSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/partSymbol"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes/partSymbol":{"title":"partSymbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/partsymbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part-symbol element indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/partSymbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"partSymbol"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV","text":"MXLPartSymbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLAttributes","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartSymbol":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part-symbol type indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score; brace is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default value. The top-staff and bottom-staff attributes are used when the brace does not extend across the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire part. For example, in a 3-staff organ part, the top-staff will typically be 1 for the right hand, while"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the bottom-staff will typically be 2 for the left hand. Staff 3 for the pedals is usually outside the brace."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"By default, the presence of a part-symbol element that does not extend across the entire part also indicates a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corresponding change in the common barlines within a part."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol","title":"MXLPartSymbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol"}]}}}